From: UniXNU-enchilada board
Subject: [PATCH] enchilada: give the boot shim a correct ARM64 image header

The OnePlus 6 ABL inflates the gzip kernel package and expects an ARM64
Image header ("ARM\x64" at offset 56, text_offset, image_size) in the
inflated blob; the community enchilada UEFI images provide it through
BootShim.S with requires_kernel_header = true.  Our first image shipped a
headerless shim (a patch dropped the header because unixnu bootimg's shim
self-check could not pass), so ABL classified the blob as a 32-bit kernel
and dead-looped before leaving fastboot.

Keep the header and fix the field that made the self-check impossible:
BootShim.S stores FD_SIZE verbatim as Image Size, but the ARM64 boot
protocol and the self-check want the size of the whole image,
shim + firmware volume.  (_Payload - _Head) is the shim length the
assembler already knows, so the field stays correct for any FD size.
---
 BootShim/BootShim.S | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/BootShim/BootShim.S b/BootShim/BootShim.S
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/BootShim/BootShim.S
+++ b/BootShim/BootShim.S
@@ -9,5 +9,5 @@
 _StackSize:
-  .quad FD_SIZE         /* Image Size */
+  .quad FD_SIZE + (_Payload - _Head) /* Image Size = shim + FD */
   .quad 0               /* Flags */
   .quad 0               /* Reserved */
   .quad 0               /* Reserved */
